test_element_angles -- LaGriT's cell angle and quality attributes,
checked against an independent computation (user, Oct 22 2026: "check
for any inconsistency or bugs in the code that computes" the ang_*,
solid angle, aspect, edge_ratio, edge_min and edge_max attributes)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_angle_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     4 decks, about 1 s
  open logs/summary.html

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_angles.py; definitions in its opening comment)

  cmo / addatt / MO / ang_mind (ang_minr, ang_maxd, ang_maxr) / ATT
      min / max dihedral angle, degrees / radians (src/cmo_addatt.f,
      dihangle_element.f, dihangle_face.f)
  cmo / addatt / MO / ang_mind_solid (ang_minr_solid, ang_maxd_solid,
      ang_maxr_solid) / ATT
      min / max solid angle at the vertices of a tet (solid_angle_lg.f)
  quality / aspect / y       aratio   (aratio_element.f and aratio_*.f)
  quality / edge_ratio / y   eratio   (aratio_element_edge.f)
  quality / edge_min / y     edgemin
  quality / edge_max / y     edgemax

  ea01_tets   213 tets: regular, corner, needle, cap, wedge, slivers,
              nearly and exactly flat tets, 200 random tets (about half
              inverted), an inverted regular tet; every value against
              the reference (1e-6)
  ea02_thin   24 slivers of height 1e-4 ... 1e-14: no angle may be lost
  ea03_solid  hex, prism, pyramid: known values
  ea04_2d     triangle, quad: known values
  Every deck: degrees = radians x 180 / pi, min <= max, eratio =
  edgemin / edgemax.

FOUND (Oct 22 2026)

  1. BUG, FIXED: in a flat or nearly flat cell rounding put the
     cosine of an angle just outside [-1, 1] (for example
     1.0000000000000002); acos gave NaN and the angle was silently
     skipped. A flat tet then had ang_mind = 458.4 and ang_maxd =
     -458.4 (the starting values +-8 radians), and a sliver of relative
     height 1e-9 or less lost its solid angles (s_maxd = -5.7e21: the
     starting value -1e20 radians). Where only some angles were lost the
     min or max was taken over the rest. Fixed by keeping the cosine in
     [-1, 1] in dihangle_face.f, dihangle_element.f (triangles and
     quads) and solid_angle_lg.f.
  2. FIXED: solid_angle_lg.f used pi = 3.14159265358, which put 5.6e-10
     "degrees" on every solid angle (the corner of a unit cube came out
     90.0000000006) and could make the solid angle of a flat vertex
     slightly negative. Now acos(-1), and the result is kept >= 0.
  3. FIXED (comment only): the descriptions of ang_maxd_solid and
     ang_minr_solid at the top of cmo_addatt.f were swapped (min / max,
     degrees / radians). The code was right.
  4. Not changed, but worth knowing:
     - The solid angle "degrees" are steradians x 180 / pi (not square
       degrees): a regular tet 31.59, a full sphere 720, the largest
       possible value (a vertex lying in the opposite face) 360. Carl's
       CAP rule s_maxd >= 170 is in these units.
     - On cells that are not tets the solid angle attributes hold a
       special value, 99999 / -99999 radians; in the degree attributes
       that becomes 5.7e6 / -5.7e6 (the warning prints the radian
       value).
     - quality / aspect is 3 r_in / R_circ for tets and 2 r_in / R_circ
       for triangles, but the shortest / longest DIAGONAL for quads and
       hexes, and 0 for prisms and pyramids. It is the absolute value,
       so an inverted tet has a positive aspect ratio (only the volume
       shows the inversion).
     - One quality command computes ONE of aspect, edge_ratio, edge_min,
       edge_max: "quality / aspect / y / edge_ratio / y" makes only
       aratio. Use one command for each.
     - The attributes quality makes are named aratio, eratio, edgemin
       and edgemax (not edge_min / edge_max).
     - Everything else agreed with the reference to 1e-9 or better on
       all 213 tets, including the inverted ones, and on the hex,
       prism, pyramid, triangle and quad.

FILES

  run_angle_tests.sh     runner (work/, logs/; WORK= and LOGS= may change them)
  make_angle_inputs.py   the meshes
  check_angles.py        reference computation, checks, logs/summary.html
  ea01-ea04 *.lgi        the decks
